Research: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/research.md Q18 (hop-by-hop headers, Proxy-Authorization, left out of AC27 and AC28)
Why this approach: the adapter only declares its header; core's newCaptureConfig already reads SecretDeclarer, so no core change. The tests run through run with a real store: AC27 scans every file under capture.dir, the database files raw and each blob decompressed through Reader.Content, and fails if no blob was scanned (both bodies are padded past InlineMax); AC28 compares the four sentinels byte for byte at upstream and at the client. AC60 uses one gateway with a small memory_limit and a deps.openStore wrapper failing SaveExchange for one path, so a stored, a dropped_memory and a store_failed capture share one log.
Alternatives rejected: forcing a queue-full drop for AC60 (needs a stuck worker and timing); the memory drop is deterministic.
Trade-off / known limit: AC60 passed on arrival, since nothing logged these values before; it guards against a future leak. The failed capture is an injected store error, not a real disk failure. Only stdout is checked for AC60; stderr stays covered by 001's TestProxy_SecretsNotLogged.
Verified by: make verify; go test -race -count=3 on TestRedact_AuthHeaders, TestRedact_ForwardedTrafficUntouched, TestCapture_SecretsNotLogged, TestAdapter_Values. Before the adapter change both TestRedact tests failed on the stored X-Api-Key sentinel (request and response headers, and gateway.db). Mutation, reverted: passing ex.Query into the sink's storeFailure log failed TestCapture_SecretsNotLogged.
